{"kind":"assert","text":"Policy decision for codex request #11385, the MCP treatment of an unusable resident advertisement. DECISION: the divergence does not stand for durable writes. cmd/gitseq-mcp must fail closed the way gs does: a present-but-untrustworthy resident.json refuses every durable write with the unusable reason, and appends nothing anywhere. THREAT MODEL: resident.json is an ordinary writable file in the meta directory; today corrupting it silently diverts state, ratify and supersede into the local fold (main.go endpoint() collapses AdvertisementUnusable into no-resident at cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:166, and submit() then folds locally and merely sets degraded:true). That is exactly the silent-custody defect the de274aac repair closed for gs, and the code comment justifying the divergence (main.go:153-160, no channel to refuse on) is wrong on its own terms: every MCP tool call returns a per-call result, and a tool error IS the refusal channel. CONTRACT, the smallest that closes the hole. (1) Missing record: unchanged, absence is the only reading that means no resident; local operation stays the baseline. (2) Unusable record, including a published record whose URL fails ValidateURL: state, ratify and supersede refuse with an error naming the reason and the recovery, no append to either log. (3) Reads (status, wait, work, artifacts, inspect, whoami) MAY still answer from the verified local fold — this read/write asymmetry is deliberate and diverges from gs, because a labeled local read misleads nobody and blinding the session would block diagnosis — but the answer must carry the unusable reason (status/degraded field), never plain no-resident. (4) presence, say and ack already fail without a resident; with an unusable record their error names the reason instead of no-resident. (5) Recovery: endpoint() already re-reads resident.json on every call while no address is cached, so fixing or deleting the record takes effect on the next tool call with no adapter restart; keep that. For explicit local choice, add a --local launch flag to cmd/gitseq-mcp mirroring gs --server - (the retired --server flag stays retired). (6) Transport failure with a TRUSTWORTHY record keeps the existing documented degraded fallback; whether that too should refuse is a separate question this decision does not reach. COMPATIBILITY: valid-advertisement and no-advertisement sessions unchanged; only sessions over a corrupt record change, from silent local fold to explicit refusal, which is the point. ARCHITECTURE: layers 3 and 7; the same head must update architecture.md:256-259, docs/reference/gs/serve.md:114-118, docs/reference/gs/status.md:249-253, and the cmd/gitseq-mcp code comment; the cloned-repo how-to sentence stating the two surfaces knowingly disagree stays true until the implementation merges and will flare and be corrected by succession then. TESTS: a class table of unusable shapes on the MCP side (mirror or extract cmd/gs/invalid_advertisement_test.go:83-179, currently package-private); refusal test per durable tool asserting the reason is named and depth is unchanged in both logs; recovery test unusable-then-fixed succeeding on the next call with no restart; a --local test showing explicit local operation over a corrupt record. SEQUENCING: implementation is authorized as a child request, filed only after the late-actor lane (17457031) merges, on the then-current cmd/gitseq-mcp and internal/app successors; that lane does not touch endpoint() or submit(), so no textual conflict is expected."}